.TH FCLOSE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
fclose \- close a Crunch file stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "int fclose(struct FILE* " stream ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR fclose ()
closes the underlying file descriptor and releases the stream.
The pointer is invalid after the call, including when closing fails.
Stream output is unbuffered, so there is no buffered output to flush.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success or
.B EOF
(\-1) with
.B errno
set on failure. A null stream fails with
.BR EINVAL .
.SH NOTES
Only open Crunch streams, including
.BR stdin ,
.BR stdout ,
.BR stderr ,
and pointers returned by
.BR fopen (3crunch),
may be used; C library streams are not compatible.
Crunch's allocator and errno are not thread-safe.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fopen (3crunch),
.BR close (3crunch)
